-- #822: a KROW DATA slot feeding an ABSTRACT head, with NO interface in the file at all.
--
-- This pins behaviour the implementation comment used to declare IMPOSSIBLE ("an
-- unscoped seam withholds nothing, so the arm never fires there").  It does fire here:
-- `e` is row-kinded from `dataParamKindsRef` — nothing to do with graded interfaces —
-- so `rowArgNamesIn` reports it, the caller withholds it from the tyvar map, and the
-- abstract-headed `f e Int` therefore meets the row-slot test with an empty graded scope.
--
-- The result is a FIX, not a leak.  Pre-#822 that withheld `e` fell through
-- `fromAstTypeE (TyVar n)`'s `optionOr (TCon n)` and became a FABRICATED RIGID
-- `TCon "e"`: `getInner` inferred as `D a b -> b e Int`, an opaque constant no caller
-- could ever satisfy.  The golden below records `D a b -> b a Int` — a real variable.
data D e f = MkD (Unit -> <e> Unit) (f e Int)

getInner : D e f -> f e Int
getInner (MkD _ x) = x
